+## Usage the afterModelResponse hook receives
+
+`afterModelResponse` is called once per user message, after the round loop exits, and reports what the turn's provider calls cost — the seam a deployer reaches for when recording an audit entry, a billing line, or a usage budget. The hook takes the turn's total as `usage` and the per-round breakdown beside it, so the signature says which number is the sum and a consumer that wants provider-call granularity keeps it.
+
+- For a turn that ran no tools, `usage` is exactly what the provider reported for its single call, so the common path reports today's number unchanged ([validated by: hands a turn with no tool calls exactly the usage it reports today](../../src/orchestration/afterModelResponseUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L112)).
+- A turn driven through two tool rounds reports the sum of every provider call's usage in the turn, not the last round's alone, so billing or budgeting from this hook no longer under-counts exactly the expensive turns ([validated by: reports the usage of every provider call in the turn, summing two tool rounds that reported different counts](../../src/orchestration/afterModelResponseUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L71)).
+- The per-round breakdown lists one `UsageMetadata` per provider call that reported usage, in round order, so a round that reported nothing contributes nothing to the total rather than poisoning it with `undefined` or `NaN`, and a turn where no round reported still reports nothing ([validated by: counts the rounds that reported usage, and reports nothing when no round did](../../src/orchestration/afterModelResponseUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L87)).
+
